Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||12-18-2001||09:50 AM||||I just finished filling out the application for my enhanced security clearance at work, they're gonna run a background check on me.. making sure I'm not a terrorist or something.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>it was kinda weird, telling them where I've been for the last 5 years, where I've lived, who I've worked for, what countries I've visited, etc.. and even after all this, I still get paid the same, I still have the same job duties, and I still can't go into restricted areas.. I think all I get is a new dot on my security badge.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> sucks working in IT sometimes, the nuclear operators have all the fun.. LOL<P>(yes, I'm at work.. and yes, I'm bored.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||6
Z||000001||The Fieromaster||12-18-2001||10:14 AM||||Hehe my buddy is a Nuclear Operator... makes nice cash too!  Im supposed to get an "IN" at the power plant soon... Starting in shipping but if all goes like he did when he started in shipping ill be an unlicensed operator also in 2 1/2 years!!<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||12-18-2001||10:44 AM||||Yeah, backround checks are fun.  When I started with NASA, the FBI did my backround check.  You can imagine the reactions I got from some of my friends who didn't know about the job when the FBI called up asking about my history!   Would have loved to get a picture of THAT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  It's always a bit interesting when the first thing you do on your first day at work is get your picture taken for your photo ID, then get fingerprinted!  So much for my career as a criminal...<P>One of the guys I worked with had Top Secret clearance so he could work on classified DOD payloads.  I don't even want to know how thorough the check was on him.  <p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||12-18-2001||10:48 AM||||Cool, I'm on the development project that's building the new nuclear operator training course for the CANDU reactor system.. All the excitement of learning this stuff, none of the fun of going on field tours and playing with the equipment  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||12-18-2001||10:55 AM||||one guy I worked with had a securtiy clearance rejected - they found out his roomate in college was arrested for possesion of drugs - that was all it took.<P> they figured he must have known what his roomate was up to.<P> another guy, Bill,  was put in for a clearance, and the FBI was trying to call the guy that shared his cubical with him at work, but Bill answered the phone.<P> The FBI guy asked for the other person, who wasnt there, so he says, well, do you know Bill?<P>  Uh, yeah I know Bill (it was Bill).<P> so the FBI asks him about 20 questions about Bill, and finally he asks, "and what is your name?"<P>  Ummmmm. Bill!<P> about 4 of us were there when the call happened, we almost died laughing.||||reg||1
